HC_BASE={{ healthchecks_base_url | quote }}
HC_PING_VERIFY={{ vault_hc_ping_verify | default('') | quote }}
HC_PING_BACKUPS={{ vault_hc_ping_backups | default('') | quote }}
HC_PING_HEARTBEAT={{ vault_hc_ping_heartbeat | default('') | quote }}
{% if vault_hc_ping_scan | default('') | length > 0 %}
HC_PING_SCAN={{ vault_hc_ping_scan | quote }}
{% endif %}
{#-
  HC_PING_SCAN is rendered CONDITIONALLY, unlike the three keys above, and both
  halves of that are deliberate.

  Only when set: roles/service_vm/tasks/verify.yml asserts that no HC_PING_*
  value is empty, by regex rather than by name, so it does not need to know
  which host uses which key. Emitting an empty HC_PING_SCAN would therefore
  fail verification on every service VM until the check exists — including
  svc-media, which never runs the scan. Omitting the line keeps that guard
  honest instead of weakening it to tolerate a blank.

  The scan is not silent without it: scan-run.sh.j2 prints a loud warning when
  HC_PING_SCAN is unset, so the missing dead-man's switch announces itself in
  the journal rather than being mistaken for a working one.

  Do NOT "tidy" this into an unconditional line to match the others. Set
  vault_hc_ping_scan and it appears on its own.
-#}
